PRESERVE / DESTROY
unit fractions: preserve forced equality witnesses; destroy lift geometry and gap interiors
binding pairs: preserve raw splice capacity; destroy third-runner blockers and overlap rank
splice obligations: preserve blocker incidence; destroy unspliced tooth components
individual teeth + endpoint events: preserve the exact target-cover predicate
tournament quotient: preserves blocker direction; destroys simultaneous connectivity

SCOPE
THM-763 makes the primitive tight branch finite, not empty.
THM-766 supplies local component-tooth cones, not global splice coherence.
The remaining lemma is: zero endpoint defect at q=13 forces one common AP scale.
